  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 103 PM CDT Wed Oct 7 2026\n\nVery little changes from previous forecasts. Mostly dry conditions \nare expected over land with low to medium rain chances over the Gulf \nwaters through Friday as Tropical Storm Isaias moves away from the \nregion. Although we will not get any direct impacts from Isaias, \nlong period swells are expected through the end of the week are \nexpected to interact with Ekman Transport to promote coastal \nflooding. Apart from the coastal flooding, moderate to high chances \nof rip curretns will also be expected. \n\nWarm temperatures will return with highs in the 90s through the week \ninto next week. Thankfully, moisture levels will be low enough to \nkeep the heat index in check. Moisture will increase next week with \nheat index values over 105 degrees return along with a moderate to \nmajor risk of heat-related impacts. Please remember to continue to \npractice heat safety: take breaks when outside, drink plenty of \nwater, and look before you lock.",
